# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial simulates the Trotterized time evolution of the tilted-field Ising model with the LTM AI-QEM function.\n"
msgstr "Sini-simulate ng tutorial na ito ang Trotterized na time evolution ng tilted-field Ising model gamit ang LTM AI-QEM function.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Originally conceptualized to understand ferromagnetism and quantum phase transitions in magnetic materials, the Ising model [[1]](#references) has become a cornerstone of modern many-body physics. At its fundamental level, the model describes a lattice of interacting spins, where each spin can occupy one of two states and interacts with its nearest neighbors. The real-time dynamics of two-dimensional Ising systems become increasingly difficult to simulate classically as the system size and evolution time increase, which makes them an important testbed for quantum simulation. Moreover, because the Hamiltonian is composed of local single-qubit fields and nearest-neighbor two-qubit interactions, its time evolution can be naturally represented with sequences of single- and two-qubit quantum gates. These properties make the model a useful benchmark for studying quantum dynamics on present-day hardware and for evaluating the effectiveness of quantum error mitigation methods.\n"
msgstr "Orihinal na binuo para unawain ang ferromagnetism at mga quantum phase transition sa mga magnetic na materyal, ang Ising model [[1]](#references) ay naging pundasyon na ng modernong many-body physics. Sa pinaka-batayang antas, inilalarawan ng model ang isang lattice ng mga nag-iinteract na spin, kung saan ang bawat spin ay maaaring nasa isa sa dalawang estado at nakikipag-interact sa mga pinakamalapit nitong kapitbahay. Habang lumalaki ang laki ng system at oras ng evolution, lalong nagiging mahirap i-simulate nang classical ang real-time dynamics ng mga two-dimensional na Ising system, kaya mahalagang testbed ang mga ito para sa quantum simulation. Bukod pa rito, dahil binubuo ang Hamiltonian ng mga lokal na single-qubit field at nearest-neighbor na two-qubit interaction, natural na mailalarawan ang time evolution nito sa pamamagitan ng mga sequence ng single- at two-qubit quantum gate. Dahil sa mga katangiang ito, kapaki-pakinabang na benchmark ang model para pag-aralan ang quantum dynamics sa kasalukuyang hardware at para suriin ang bisa ng mga paraan ng quantum error mitigation.\n"

