# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Define the Hamiltonian {#step-2-define-the-hamiltonian}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: Tukuyin ang Hamiltonian {#step-2-define-the-hamiltonian}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Define the Ising Hamiltonian with the Qiskit `SparsePauliOp` class. To do this, specify the angles `theta_x` $(\\theta_x)$, `theta_z` $(\\theta_z)$, and `theta_zz` $(\\theta_{zz})$, which are related to the transverse field strength (`g_x`), the longitudinal field strength (`g_z`), and the Ising coupling strength (`J`), respectively. Specifically, $\\theta_x=2g_x\\Delta{t}$, $\\theta_z=2g_z\\Delta{t}$, and $\\theta_{zz}=2J\\Delta{t}$.\n"
msgstr "Tukuyin ang Ising Hamiltonian gamit ang Qiskit `SparsePauliOp` class. Para gawin ito, tukuyin ang mga anggulong `theta_x` $(\\theta_x)$, `theta_z` $(\\theta_z)$, at `theta_zz` $(\\theta_{zz})$, na may kaugnayan sa transverse field strength (`g_x`), longitudinal field strength (`g_z`), at Ising coupling strength (`J`), ayon sa pagkakasunod. Partikular, $\\theta_x=2g_x\\Delta{t}$, $\\theta_z=2g_z\\Delta{t}$, at $\\theta_{zz}=2J\\Delta{t}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Use the `SparsePauliOp.from_sparse_list` method to instantiate the transverse field Hamiltonian (`Hx`), the longitudinal field Hamiltonian (`Hz`), and the coupling Hamiltonian (`Hzz`). The `SparsePauliOp.from_sparse_list` method takes as input a list of tuples. Each tuple contains a Pauli string, the indices of the qubits that the Pauli operators in the string act on, and the coefficient of the Pauli string. For more details, see the [`SparsePauliOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp) API documentation. The qubit indices come from the `problem_nodes` and `problem_edges` objects defined earlier. The full tilted-field Ising Hamiltonian is the sum of these three Hamiltonians.\n"
msgstr "Gamitin ang `SparsePauliOp.from_sparse_list` method para i-instantiate ang transverse field Hamiltonian (`Hx`), ang longitudinal field Hamiltonian (`Hz`), at ang coupling Hamiltonian (`Hzz`). Ang `SparsePauliOp.from_sparse_list` method ay tumatanggap bilang input ng listahan ng mga tuple. Ang bawat tuple ay naglalaman ng Pauli string, ang mga index ng mga qubit na kinikilos ng mga Pauli operator sa string, at ang coefficient ng Pauli string. Para sa karagdagang detalye, tingnan ang [`SparsePauliOp`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.quantum_info.SparsePauliOp) API documentation. Ang mga qubit index ay galing sa mga `problem_nodes` at `problem_edges` object na tinukoy kanina. Ang buong tilted-field Ising Hamiltonian ay ang kabuuan ng tatlong Hamiltonian na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Construct the Trotterized quantum circuit {#step-3-construct-the-trotterized-quantum-circuit}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Buuin ang Trotterized na quantum circuit {#step-3-construct-the-trotterized-quantum-circuit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now, construct the quantum circuit that corresponds to the Trotterized evolution of the qubits in `problem_nodes` under the tilted-field Ising model. To simulate the time evolution, construct a sequence of quantum circuits with an increasing number of Trotter steps (for example, 1, 2, and 3 steps). Set the number of Trotter steps, `num_trotter_steps`, to 10, and create a range, `trotter_steps`, that contains the numbers from 1 to `num_trotter_steps`.\n"
msgstr "Ngayon, buuin ang quantum circuit na tumutugma sa Trotterized na evolution ng mga qubit sa `problem_nodes` sa ilalim ng tilted-field Ising model. Para i-simulate ang time evolution, bumuo ng sequence ng mga quantum circuit na may dumaraming bilang ng Trotter step (halimbawa, 1, 2, at 3 step). Itakda ang bilang ng Trotter step, `num_trotter_steps`, sa 10, at gumawa ng range, `trotter_steps`, na naglalaman ng mga numero mula 1 hanggang `num_trotter_steps`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To construct the quantum circuit for a specific number of Trotter steps, use the Qiskit [`evolved_operator_ansatz`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.evolved_operator_ansatz) function. This function takes as input the tilted-field Ising Hamiltonian, defined earlier as a `SparsePauliOp` object, and outputs the quantum circuit that corresponds to the evolution. Store the circuits in a dictionary, `trotter_circ_dict`, whose keys are the numbers of Trotter steps and whose values are the corresponding quantum circuits. The code inserts barriers between Trotter steps only to make the circuit diagram easier to read. You can remove the code that inserts the barriers.\n"
msgstr "Para buuin ang quantum circuit para sa partikular na bilang ng Trotter step, gamitin ang Qiskit [`evolved_operator_ansatz`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit/qiskit.circuit.library.evolved_operator_ansatz) function. Tumatanggap ang function na ito bilang input ng tilted-field Ising Hamiltonian, na tinukoy kanina bilang isang `SparsePauliOp` object, at naglalabas ng quantum circuit na tumutugma sa evolution. I-store ang mga circuit sa isang dictionary, `trotter_circ_dict`, na ang mga key ay ang bilang ng mga Trotter step at ang mga value ay ang mga katumbas na quantum circuit. Naglalagay lang ang code ng mga barrier sa pagitan ng mga Trotter step para mas madaling basahin ang circuit diagram. Maaari mong alisin ang code na naglalagay ng mga barrier.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that `evolved_operator_ansatz` outputs a parameterized quantum circuit with a parameter `t` that takes the value of $\\Delta{t}$ in the evolution operator. Because the definitions of the `theta` angles already include $\\Delta{t}$, set all parameters to `t=1`.\n"
msgstr "Tandaan na ang `evolved_operator_ansatz` ay nag-o-output ng parameterized quantum circuit na may parameter na `t` na may halaga ng $\\Delta{t}$ sa evolution operator. Dahil kasama na sa mga depinisyon ng mga anggulong `theta` ang $\\Delta{t}$, itakda ang lahat ng parameter sa `t=1`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/trotterized-time-evolution-ltm/extracted-outputs/8c0f5da2-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/trotterized-time-evolution-ltm/extracted-outputs/8c0f5da2-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The exponentials of the Pauli operators $X$, $Z$, and ${Z}{Z}$ are the following rotation gates:\n"
"$$\n"
"R_x(\\theta_x)=e^{-i{\\frac{\\theta_x}{2}}X}\n"
"\\quad;\\quad\n"
"R_z(\\theta_z)=e^{-i{\\frac{\\theta_z}{2}}Z}\n"
"\\quad;\\quad\n"
"R_{zz}(\\theta_{zz})=e^{-i{\\frac{\\theta_{zz}}{2}}ZZ}\n"
"$$\n"
"So the Trotterized evolution becomes:\n"
"$$\n"
"e^{iHt} \\approx \\Bigg[\n"
"\\bigg(\\prod_{k\\in{N}}{R_x(\\theta_x)}\\bigg)\n"
"\\bigg(\\prod_{k\\in{N}}{R_z(\\theta_z)}\\bigg)\n"
"\\bigg(\\prod_{\\begin{matrix} {(k,l)}{\\in}{E} \\\\ {k<l} \\end{matrix}}{R_{zz}(\\theta_{zz})}\\bigg)\n"
"\\Bigg]^r\n"
"$$\n"
"The previous circuit diagram shows the repeated pattern of the circuit. Each step contains $R_x(\\theta_x=0.53)$ and $R_z(\\theta_z=0.1)$ gates on each qubit, and an $R_{zz}(\\theta_{zz}=1)$ gate between each pair of qubits where two-qubit interactions are allowed.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang mga exponential ng mga Pauli operator na $X$, $Z$, at ${Z}{Z}$ ay ang mga sumusunod na rotation gate:\n"
"$$\n"
"R_x(\\theta_x)=e^{-i{\\frac{\\theta_x}{2}}X}\n"
"\\quad;\\quad\n"
"R_z(\\theta_z)=e^{-i{\\frac{\\theta_z}{2}}Z}\n"
"\\quad;\\quad\n"
"R_{zz}(\\theta_{zz})=e^{-i{\\frac{\\theta_{zz}}{2}}ZZ}\n"
"$$\n"
"Kaya ang Trotterized evolution ay nagiging:\n"
"$$\n"
"e^{iHt} \\approx \\Bigg[\n"
"\\bigg(\\prod_{k\\in{N}}{R_x(\\theta_x)}\\bigg)\n"
"\\bigg(\\prod_{k\\in{N}}{R_z(\\theta_z)}\\bigg)\n"
"\\bigg(\\prod_{\\begin{matrix} {(k,l)}{\\in}{E} \\\\ {k<l} \\end{matrix}}{R_{zz}(\\theta_{zz})}\\bigg)\n"
"\\Bigg]^r\n"
"$$\n"
"Ipinapakita ng nakaraang circuit diagram ang paulit-ulit na pattern ng circuit. Bawat step ay naglalaman ng mga gate na $R_x(\\theta_x=0.53)$ at $R_z(\\theta_z=0.1)$ sa bawat Qubit, at isang gate na $R_{zz}(\\theta_{zz}=1)$ sa pagitan ng bawat pares ng Qubit kung saan pinapayagan ang two-qubit interaction.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Construct the observable for average magnetization {#step-4-construct-the-observable-for-average-magnetization}"
msgstr "Step 4: Buuin ang observable para sa average magnetization {#step-4-construct-the-observable-for-average-magnetization}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The observable for the average magnetization is as follows:\n"
"$$\n"
"H_M = \\frac{1}{|N|}\\Bigg(\\sum_{k\\in{N}}{Z_k}\\Bigg)\n"
"$$\n"
"where $|N|$ is the size of the set $N$. Use the `SparsePauliOp` class again to define the observable `Hm`, which corresponds to the average magnetization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang observable para sa average magnetization ay ang sumusunod:\n"
"$$\n"
"H_M = \\frac{1}{|N|}\\Bigg(\\sum_{k\\in{N}}{Z_k}\\Bigg)\n"
"$$\n"
"kung saan ang $|N|$ ay ang laki ng set na $N$. Gamitin muli ang class na `SparsePauliOp` para ilarawan ang observable na `Hm`, na tumutugma sa average magnetization.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 5: Compute the expectation value with the LTM AI-QEM function {#step-5-compute-the-expectation-value-with-the-ltm-ai-qem-function}"
msgstr "Step 5: Kalkulahin ang expectation value gamit ang LTM AI-QEM function {#step-5-compute-the-expectation-value-with-the-ltm-ai-qem-function}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute the expectation value of the average magnetization observable, `Hm`, for each circuit in `trotter_circ_dict`. To do this, transpile each circuit, apply the layout of the transpiled circuit to `Hm`, and create a list of primitive unified blocs (PUBs). Each PUB contains the transpiled circuit for a specific number of Trotter steps and the corresponding observable.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang expectation value ng observable ng average magnetization, ang `Hm`, para sa bawat circuit sa `trotter_circ_dict`. Para magawa ito, i-transpile ang bawat circuit, i-apply ang layout ng na-transpile na circuit sa `Hm`, at gumawa ng listahan ng primitive unified blocs (PUBs). Bawat PUB ay naglalaman ng na-transpile na circuit para sa isang partikular na bilang ng Trotter step at ng katumbas na observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then pass the list of PUBs to `ltm_function`, which you defined at the beginning of the tutorial. You can either pass transpiled circuits with the layout applied to the corresponding observables, as shown in the following code, or pass the transpilation options through `options`. If you pass the transpilation options, the function transpiles the circuits and applies the layout to the observables.\n"
msgstr "Pagkatapos, ipasa ang listahan ng mga PUB sa `ltm_function`, na dinefine mo sa simula ng tutorial. Maaari mong ipasa ang mga na-transpile na circuit na may layout na naka-apply na sa mga katumbas na observable, tulad ng ipinapakita sa sumusunod na code, o ipasa ang mga opsyon sa transpilation sa pamamagitan ng `options`. Kung ipapasa mo ang mga opsyon sa transpilation, tina-transpile ng function ang mga circuit at ina-apply ang layout sa mga observable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare against ZNE {#compare-against-zne}"
msgstr "Ihambing sa ZNE {#compare-against-zne}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compute the average magnetization with the zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) method available in `qiskit-ibm-runtime`. Define the `EstimatorV2` primitive to compute the expectation values, and enable ZNE error mitigation with `estimator.options`, as shown in the following code.\n"
msgstr "Kalkulahin ang average magnetization gamit ang zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) method na available sa `qiskit-ibm-runtime`. Idefine ang primitive na `EstimatorV2` para kalkulahin ang mga expectation value, at i-enable ang ZNE error mitigation gamit ang `estimator.options`, tulad ng ipinapakita sa sumusunod na code.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Sparse Pauli dynamics results {#sparse-pauli-dynamics-results}"
msgstr "Mga resulta ng sparse Pauli dynamics {#sparse-pauli-dynamics-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses the classical sparse Pauli dynamics (SPD) algorithm [[2, 3]](#references) to evaluate the average magnetization. SPD was previously applied to simulate the kicked transverse-field Ising model experiment in [[4]](#references). This tutorial treats the SPD results as ideal, and compares the results from the LTM AI-QEM function against them. To keep this tutorial simple, it doesn't include the code that generates the SPD results. Instead, the results are provided in the `spd_results` list. The implementation of the SPD algorithm by its authors is available in [[5]](#references).\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng tutorial na ito ang klasikal na sparse Pauli dynamics (SPD) algorithm [[2, 3]](#references) para i-evaluate ang average magnetization. Dati nang na-apply ang SPD para i-simulate ang eksperimento ng kicked transverse-field Ising model sa [[4]](#references). Itinuturing ng tutorial na ito ang mga resulta ng SPD bilang ideal, at inihahambing dito ang mga resulta mula sa LTM AI-QEM function. Para manatiling simple ang tutorial na ito, hindi nito isinasama ang code na gumagawa ng mga resulta ng SPD. Sa halip, ibinibigay ang mga resulta sa listahang `spd_results`. Ang implementasyon ng SPD algorithm ng mga may-akda nito ay available sa [[5]](#references).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare the results {#compare-the-results}"
msgstr "Ihambing ang mga resulta {#compare-the-results}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To compare the mitigation methods, plot the results from LTM AI-QEM, ZNE, and the unmitigated hardware execution against the SPD reference for each number of Trotter steps. The code also prints a table of key performance metrics for a quantitative comparison.\n"
msgstr "Para ihambing ang mga paraan ng mitigation, i-plot ang mga resulta mula sa LTM AI-QEM, ZNE, at sa unmitigated na pagpapatakbo sa hardware laban sa SPD reference para sa bawat bilang ng Trotter step. Nagpiprint din ang code ng talahanayan ng mga pangunahing sukatan ng performance para sa kwantitatibong paghahambing.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/trotterized-time-evolution-ltm/extracted-outputs/84a5d8f2-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/trotterized-time-evolution-ltm/extracted-outputs/84a5d8f2-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-20
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The LTM AI-QEM results closely follow the SPD results for all Trotter steps. LTM AI-QEM reduces the mean absolute error (MAE) to 0.055, compared with 0.249 for ZNE and 0.266 for the unmitigated results. This is a 79.2% improvement over the unmitigated results, whereas ZNE provides a 6.4% improvement. The corresponding root mean squared error (RMSE) values are 0.062 for LTM AI-QEM, 0.270 for ZNE, and 0.285 for the unmitigated results. LTM AI-QEM achieves this improvement without additional QPU time, because the correction is applied during post-processing.\n"
msgstr "Malapit na sinusundan ng mga resulta ng LTM AI-QEM ang mga resulta ng SPD para sa lahat ng Trotter step. Binabawasan ng LTM AI-QEM ang mean absolute error (MAE) sa 0.055, kumpara sa 0.249 para sa ZNE at 0.266 para sa mga unmitigated na resulta. Ito ay 79.2% na pagbuti kumpara sa mga unmitigated na resulta, samantalang ang ZNE ay nagbibigay ng 6.4% na pagbuti. Ang katumbas na mga halaga ng root mean squared error (RMSE) ay 0.062 para sa LTM AI-QEM, 0.270 para sa ZNE, at 0.285 para sa mga unmitigated na resulta. Nakakamit ng LTM AI-QEM ang pagbuting ito nang walang karagdagang QPU time, dahil ang correction ay ina-apply sa post-processing.\n"

